            'Consensus is not a simple majority vote. It is a structured analysis of agreement across claims, not just surface-level similarity. Two responses can say the same thing in different words, and two responses can look similar while containing materially different facts. Claim-level analysis, as in PromptQuorum’s Atomic Facts and Overlap Mapping analyses, extracts and compares claims individually.',
