      intro: 'Three different regulatory approaches to AI now run in parallel. The EU enforces a binding, risk-based AI Act with a delayed high-risk timetable, the US relies on executive action, sector rules and a contested patchwork of state laws, and China regulates through filing, security and content-labeling measures. This divide shapes AI deployment, data residency and vendor strategy.',
